description: Clean Architecture, DDD and Ports and Adapters conventions for this project
alwaysApply: true
---

# Architecture Rules

- Organize code first by architectural layer, then by domain module.
- Keep `domain` independent from `application`, `presentation`, `infra` and `main`.
- Keep `application` independent from `presentation`, `infra` and `main`.
- Use use cases for application orchestration.
- Use `Either` for expected domain/application errors.
- Do not wrap use cases in generic `try/catch`.
- Let unexpected technical errors bubble to `SafeUseCase` in `main`.
- Keep repository interfaces near the domain module they represent.
- Put concrete adapters in `infra/adapters`.
- Put composition, factories, route registration and framework wiring in `main`.
- Add abstractions only when they match an existing pattern or remove real duplication.

# Module Organization

- Do not create global folders like `domain/entities` or `application/use-cases`.
- Domain files go under `domain/<module>`.
- Application files go under `application/<module>`.
- HTTP files go under `presentation/http/<module>`.
- Persistence adapters go under `infra/adapters/persistence/<technology>/<module>`.
- Main factories mirror what they compose:
  - `main/factories/application/<module>`
  - `main/factories/presentation/http/<module>`
  - `main/factories/infra/persistence/<module>`

Example for a `product` module:

```txt
domain/product/entities/product.entity.ts
application/product/use-cases/create-product.usecase.ts
presentation/http/product/controllers/create-product.controller.ts
infra/adapters/persistence/memory/product/memory-product.repository.ts
```
